# SPL USB boot profile -- COMPOSITION NOTES ONLY.
#
# This fragment is no longer the build recipe for any shipping target.  Since
# 584916c96db the open chain is ONE defconfig per board --
# configs/libretech-cc_libre_defconfig (DDR3) and
# configs/libretech-cc_v2_libre_defconfig (DDR4) -- which is what LBS names in
# configs/aml-s905x-cc{,-v2}-libre and what every hardware result on the open
# chain was measured from.  Do NOT stack this on the product defconfig and
# expect the tested binary: it predates the DDR4 map, the FIT staging address
# and the size repair, none of which are here.
#
# It is kept because the single-file defconfigs are savedefconfig output and
# therefore say WHAT is set, never WHY.  The reasoning below -- the 0xb000
# ceiling, the console-cost measurement, the MMC drop -- has no other home.
#
# The TPL geometry that used to live at the end of this file moved to
# configs/tpl-spl-chain.config, which is where the chain recipe now is.
#
# Historic recipe, for reading old logs only -- AND IT NO LONGER LINKS:
#   make libretech-cc_defconfig spl-usb.config
#
# Measured 2026-08-30 at v2026.07/lc-master e8fba1cfb00.  That stack stops with
#
#   spl/u-boot-spl.bin exceeds file size limit:
#     limit:  0xb000 bytes
#     actual: 0xb2eb bytes
#     excess: 0x2eb bytes
#
# The product defconfig brings SPL features the single-file -libre defconfigs
# deliberately drop.  Against libretech-cc_libre_defconfig the generated
# .config differs in exactly CONFIG_SPL_MMC, CONFIG_SPL_MMC_TINY and
# CONFIG_SPL_LEGACY_BLOCK -- and in nothing the -libre profile has that this
# stack lacks -- and the SPL is 45803 B against that profile's 38107 B.
# Nothing here will be trimmed to make the old stack fit again: the
# shipping recipe is configs/libretech-cc_libre_defconfig on its own.
#
# Builds the SPL that takes the DWC2 over from the BootROM and
# receives a FIT into DRAM over HS bulk.  Leaves every product
# feature of the base defconfig alone -- the SPL is a separate
# binary and does not require turning anything off.
CONFIG_SPL_MESON_USB_BOOT=y
CONFIG_SPL=y
CONFIG_SPL_GPIO=y
CONFIG_SPL_LIBCOMMON_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_SPL_LIBGENERIC_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_SPL_TEXT_BASE=0xd9001000
CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=912
CONFIG_DRAM_2T_MODE=y
CONFIG_SPL_MMC=y
CONFIG_SPL_SERIAL=y
CONFIG_SPL_HAVE_INIT_STACK=y
CONFIG_SPL_STACK=0xd900ff00
CONFIG_SPL_SYS_MALLOC_F_LEN=0x1000
CONFIG_SPL_LOAD_FIT=y
# 0x02000000, NOT 0x05000000.  On GXL 0x05000000 is three things at once:
# the fixed FIT buffer board_spl_fit_buffer_addr() returns (CONFIG_TEXT_BASE
# + 0x4000000, which is exactly 0x05000000 on the v1), the DT reserve
# secmon@5000000 (meson-gx.dtsi, no-map), and 1 MiB below BL31's load and
# entry 0x05100000 (meson-gxl-u-boot.dtsi).  Staging there survives only
# while the FIT stays small enough to reach none of them.  Matches
# configs/libretech-cc_libre_defconfig (220f5f01a17) and spl-g12a.config.
CONFIG_SPL_LOAD_FIT_ADDRESS=0x02000000
# CONFIG_SPL_FIT_IMAGE_POST_PROCESS is not set
# 0xb000, not 0xc000: 0xc000 is the SIGNED size (0x1000 amlimage header +
# 0xb000 payload).  Too high and an over-size SPL only fails at mkimage.
CONFIG_SPL_SIZE_LIMIT=0xb000
CONFIG_SPL_MAX_SIZE=0xb000
CONFIG_SPL_PAD_TO=0x1fe00
CONFIG_SPL_HAS_BSS_LINKER_SECTION=y
CONFIG_SPL_BSS_START_ADDR=0xd900d000
CONFIG_SPL_BSS_MAX_SIZE=0x1000
CONFIG_SPL_LEGACY_IMAGE_FORMAT=y
CONFIG_SPL_RAM_DEVICE=y
CONFIG_SPL_SYS_MALLOC_SIMPLE=y
# CONFIG_SPL_SHARES_INIT_SP_ADDR is not set
CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_USE_SECTOR=y
CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR=0x100
# CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_FS_BOOT is not set
CONFIG_SPL_MMC_TINY=y
CONFIG_SPL_ATF=y
CONFIG_SPL_OF_CONTROL=y
CONFIG_SPL_DM=y
CONFIG_SPL_OF_TRANSLATE=y
# This does NOT make the SPL silent, and the next person to read it should not
# spend a rig cycle re-deriving that.  It drops the serial *uclass* -- the
# probe/bind path and preloader_console_init(), which is compiled out with it --
# but common/console.o is still linked (common/Makefile keys it on
# CONFIG_$(PHASE_)SERIAL, which spl-usb.config sets), and its putc() falls
# through to printch() whenever GD_FLG_SERIAL_READY is clear:
#
#	/* if we don't have a console yet, use the debug UART */
#	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DEBUG_UART) && !(gd->flags & GD_FLG_SERIAL_READY))
#		printch(c);
#
# With no uclass nothing ever sets that flag, so the branch is unconditional in
# practice, and CONFIG_DEBUG_UART=y + DEBUG_UART_MESON + DEBUG_UART_BASE
# (0xc81004c0, the GXL AO UART) come in from libretech-cc_defconfig.  Verified
# in the linked binary, not inferred: putc() disassembles to a poll of
# 0xc81004cc bit 21 and a store to 0xc81004c0, with the LF->CRLF fixup inline.
# So printf()/puts()/SPL_BANNER_PRINT all reach the AO UART already.
#
# On top of that the SPL emits bare-metal UART breadcrumbs that owe nothing to
# any of this: save_boot_params (arch/arm/mach-meson/spl-boot-debug.S) writes
# "\r\nSPL\r\n" as the SPL's first instructions, before clocks or DDR, and
# arch/arm/mach-meson/spl.c early_puts()es "1" "2" "4" "5" "USB" "FIT" along the
# product path.  A USB boot that produces ZERO bytes on UART_AO therefore means
# the SPL did not run (or the capture is not on UART_AO) -- it does not mean
# console support is missing.  Diagnose that before touching this file.
#
# Turning the uclass back on is not an option here, it is a 1 KiB overspend.
# Measured 2026-08-07 on 06a59ff1451, gcc 14.2.0, spl/u-boot-spl.bin:
#
#	board                    base      +SPL_SERIAL_PRESENT=y   vs 0xb000
#	libretech-cc_defconfig    45035 B   46091 B (+1056)         1035 B over
#	libretech-cc_v2_defconfig 45043 B   46099 B (+1056)         1043 B over
#
# (ld reports "region `.sram' overflowed by 232 bytes" -- that is only the tail
# __u_boot_list section, not the total, and reading it as the shortfall
# understates the cost by 4x.  The totals above come from relinking with
# SPL_MAX_SIZE raised, which is a measurement trick only: the amlimage payload
# is fixed at 0xb000 and a larger SPL cannot be USB-booted at all.)
#
# Nothing in this file is worth 1 KiB -- SPL_BANNER_PRINT, SPL_CRC32 and
# SPL_DM_USB are all load-bearing for the USB loop and were already shown to
# regress it when trimmed.  If a full console is ever genuinely needed, the
# place it fits is the DRAM stage of the TPL->SPL chain
# (CONFIG_MESON_GX_XPL_CHAIN), where the 0xb000 cap binds the TPL and the SPL
# has no cap at all -- not here.
# CONFIG_SPL_SERIAL_PRESENT is not set
# CONFIG_SPL_SHA1 is not set

# Sitting on the product defconfig the SPL inherits these; none are
# used by the USB boot path, and the amlimage payload cap is 0xb000.

# Matched to the SPL config of the build measured clean
# (6/6 and 8/8 cycles); see the commit message.
# CONFIG_SPLASH_SOURCE is not set
# CONFIG_SPL_DM_I2C is not set

CONFIG_SPL_BANNER_PRINT=y
CONFIG_SPL_CRC32=y
CONFIG_SPL_DM_USB=y
# CONFIG_SPL_SHA256 is not set	# payload arrives over USB; SPL does not hash it
# CONFIG_SPL_SHA256_LEGACY is not set	# ditto
# CONFIG_SPL_EFI_PARTITION is not set	# no partition is parsed on this path
# CONFIG_SPL_PARTITION_UUIDS is not set	# ditto
# CONFIG_SPL_LIB_UUID is not set	# ditto

# The TPL geometry block that used to be here is now in
# configs/tpl-spl-chain.config.  It was moved because it is chain-only: with it
# here, every build of this fragment produced a TPL binary nobody used, and the
# single-file -libre defconfigs -- which are savedefconfig of this fragment on
# the product defconfig, taken BEFORE the chain existed -- never carried it
# anyway.  Keeping the chain symbols with the chain recipe means the shipping
# defconfig stays a pure single-stage config and the chain is exactly one
# fragment away from it.
